; M4 gate: the block edge's three jobs on one voice (driver.md §5, D10 §1.5).
; The sample loops from a point that is NOT its start, so WRAP differs from the
; note's own source address and the rounding contract has to hold both ends:
; the first pass plays [0, loop-end) and every later one [loop-start, loop-end).
; The gated note keys off mid-loop, which is a RETARGET to the sample's real end
; with WRAP = silence — the tail plays out once and the voice parks.
(def pad (sample :file "pad.wav" :loop-start 16ms :loop-end 45ms))
(def pcm-voices 1)
(pcm1 pad :mode loop :tempo 120 :oct 4 :len 2 :vel 15
  c :gate* 0.5 e c _)
